e` (exactly one added line,\n'pinned_ticket_read_failed') and folded it into this change via a scripted\nrebase-edit of the 0aee commit (Change-Id preserved), replaying the 5f96 and\nguardrail commits on top. Local `--check` and full test_api_surface_gate.py (14)\nnow pass. Re-pushed as patchset 2.","timestamp":1788072187805679001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788056673183653005,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"681de8ac-532c-4fd7-acaf-3b51d901805f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"98f4-32b6-2b7f-4b6a"},{"link_uuid":"70b03c6c-c0c2-4e26-ad5b-ab7d480683a9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2f97-3e28-0a1b-4a5c"}],"description":"## Finding (audit of epic 3405-c0b7)\n**Site:** `src/rebar/_reads.py:99` sets `err.error_code = \"pinned_ticket_read_failed\"`, returned verbatim by `error_code_for` branch 5 (the `exc.error_code` passthrough). But `pinned_ticket_read_failed` is NOT a member of `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (`src/rebar/_errors.py:48-66`).\n\n**Problem:** the code itself is descriptive (NOT misleading). The defect is a vocabulary-completeness gap: `error_code_for`'s own docstring says it \"Returns a stable vocabulary code (one of KNOWN_ERROR_CODES)\", but this passthrough emits a code outside that set. Any consumer that validates the returned code against `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (the documented contract) would reject a legitimately-emitted code, or fall back to treating it as unknown.\n\n**Observable vs latent:** OBSERVABLE — emitted on the pinned-ticket read failure path; reaches the MCP envelope guard and the CLI reader envelope.\n\n**Proposed fix — READY-TO-FIX (reuse existing, no design decision):** add `\"pinned_ticket_read_failed\"` to the `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` frozenset so the emitted vocabulary and the declared vocabulary agree. (Alternatively, add a contract test that asserts every `err.error_code` string assigned in the tree is a member of `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` — see the epic's prevention recommendation.) Low priority; not misleading, but it violates the stated vocabulary contract.\n\n**caused_by / class:** vocabulary drift, not the `llm_unavailable` pattern.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `pinned_ticket_read_failed` is a member of the `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` frozenset in `src/rebar/_errors.py`, so the emitted vocabulary and the declared vocabulary agree.\n- [x] The `pinned_ticket_read_failed` code emitted on the pinned-ticket read-failure path is proven to be a `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` member through the real read surface by the held-out oracle `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_pinned_ticket_read_failed_0aee.py`.\n- [x] The public-surface drift gate stays green — the pinned constant `rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` gains the new member in the committed baseline `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`; checked: `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check` exits 0.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_pinned_ticket_read_failed_0aee.py -q`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py -q`\n- `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_errors.py","reason":"Register pinned_ticket_read_failed in KNOWN_ERROR_CODES (emitted but unregistered vocabulary gap)"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_pinned_ticket_read_failed_0aee.py","reason":"Held-out oracle: the emitted pinned_ticket_read_failed code is a KNOWN_ERROR_CODES member through the real read surface"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3405-c0b7-0436-4b46"],["relates_to","2f97-3e28-0a1b-4a5c"],["relates_to","98f4-32b6-2b7f-4b6a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3405-c0b7-0436-4b46","parent_status_uuid":"a5900b5e-6068-47e6-b816-3f88db740d40","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["error-taxonomy","ready-to-fix"],"ticket_id":"0aee-a70d-045b-48a1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"pinned_ticket_read_failed is emitted but absent from KNOWN_ERROR_CODES (vocabulary-contract gap)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2ffd211e-7ce2-42bf-ab10-b43a066d69db","681de8ac-532c-4fd7-acaf-3b51d901805f","f37923b4-d268-43e4-a99d-ca1be129e99f","70b03c6c-c0c2-4e26-ad5b-ab7d480683a9","5ad29913-a2f8-41fa-995e-d2103dffa53a","8b44e5d6-5fef-45d8-a9f5-00f35628e70c","11ff40b9-d19c-4fd0-8776-2dec136417af","49a5af11-8980-4488-a4d5-88764def58a0","e4a41680-ab56-43b5-9889-7be29d73a95d","a5900b5e-6068-47e6-b816-3f88db740d40","01699d4b-d8bf-477a-af52-36c646046ac6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788087217141260001,"uuid":"b049b623-fa83-43c9-9578-2bd7146de57f"}